Message-ID: <l_B67M0sLAQ.q7QlWH3HBgAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <l_B67M0sLAQ._MaO_ybHBgAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
References: <l_B67M0sLAQ._MaO_ybHBgAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/l_B67M0sLAQ/m/q7QlWH3HBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

you just need to create a matrix that describes how landmarks are paired. E.g., if your landmarks are ordered such that 1 is on left, 2 is on right, 3 is on left 4 is on right so forth.. you can create these vectors:
left <- c(1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13)
right <-c(2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14)
and then assign the land.pairs to cbind(left, right)

