Subject: What is the difference between two formulae for morphol.disparity
Message-ID: <jgx1eImagS8.qPn_Ey6-AwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/jgx1eImagS8/m/qPn_Ey6-AwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all,

I would like to ask what is the difference between the following two lines of code below:

morphol.disparity(coords ~ 1, groups= ~ species*site,
data = gdf, iter = 999, print.progress = FALSE)

morphol.disparity(coords ~ species*site, groups= ~species*site,
data = gdf, iter = 999, print.progress = FALSE)

These two formula differ only by the specifications on the right side of the formula. I would like to ask how should they be interpreted.

Best regards,
Lv

From uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com  Tue Sep 29 11:30:33 2020
From: uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com (Mike Collyer)
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2020 11:30:33 +0000
Subject: Re: [geomorph-r-package] What is the difference between two formulae for morphol.disparity
Message-ID: <jgx1eImagS8.9f0YOYy_AwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <jgx1eImagS8.qPn_Ey6-AwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
References: <jgx1eImagS8.qPn_Ey6-AwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/jgx1eImagS8/m/9f0YOYy_AwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lv,

The former analyses residuals from a model that estimates only an overall mean; the latter analyses residuals from a model that estimates species:site means.  The former will have larger residuals (in terms of distance from estimates) than the latter.  An analysis performed for the former will will ask the question, “Do any species:site groups diverge more from the overall mean than others?”  An analysis on the latter will ask, “Do species:site groups differ in the spread of values around their means.

Hope that helps!

Mike

